    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a new pilot and I'm worried I'm leaning too hard into some clichés. Can you look over these four character sketches and tell me if any of them feel like \"tropes\" to you? Also, just based on their vibe, which ones feel more like they belong in a gritty crime/street drama versus a polished, high-society drama?\n\n1. Marcus: Mid-40s, extremely sharp, always in a tailored suit. He's a venture capitalist who manages high-stakes mergers. He's very calm under pressure.\n2. Jace: Early 20s, grew up in a rough neighborhood, very street-smart, quick to react to threats. He's currently trying to stay out of trouble but keeps getting pulled back in.\n3. Hana: Late 20s, brilliant software engineer, very disciplined and quiet. She's often the smartest person in the room but prefers to stay in the background.\n4. Elena: 30s, old money, very refined manners. She's part of a prominent political family and knows exactly how to navigate a gala or a press conference.\n\nDo these feel original enough, or am I just hitting the same old beats? And which genres do you see them fitting into?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
